      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: `value.to_str()` allocates an owned `String`, and if `escape_ninja_token` returns `Cow::Borrowed`, `.into_owned()` will allocate a second `String` with the same contents. You can avoid the second allocation by matching on the `Cow`:\n```rust\nlet s \u003d value.to_str();\nmatch escape_ninja_token(\u0026s) {\n    Cow::Borrowed(_) \u003d\u003e Cow::Owned(s),\n    Cow::Owned(escaped) \u003d\u003e Cow::Owned(escaped),\n}\n```",
      "range": {
