      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T07:22:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The comment says this returns the `minimum` number of escape characters, but `token.len() + n_escapes + 2` actually acts as a conservative `maximum` (upper bound) of extra characters needed. \n\nBecause of this, `String::with_capacity(token.len() + n)` will allocate `token.len() * 2 + n_escapes + 2`, which is roughly double the required memory.\n\nAdditionally, the inline comment (`// Assume there must be a closing character escaped as well.`) suggests you might have intended to add a small constant (like `1` or `2`) for the closing character rather than adding the entire `token.len()`.\n\nConsider updating the comment to clarify that this returns an upper bound / capacity estimate, or fix the calculation if `token.len()` was a typo.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "da6331d304967d37316bfb305e2373ddb194ed15",
