      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: If `token` is an empty string, `escape_mode` returns `(false, 0)`. Then `escape_ninja_token` returns `Cow::Borrowed(\"\")`. However, an empty string argument passed to a shell will be completely dropped unless it is quoted (e.g. `\"\"`). Consider handling empty strings explicitly so they get quoted:\n```rust\nif token.is_empty() {\n    return (true, 2);\n}\n```",
